Z||000000||gmata||07-24-2000||12:34 PM||||I just had my gaskets in the Exhaust Manifold replaced.  When replacing the gaskets would a mechanic be required to remove the throttle cable?  It seems that when I left the shop, the car wasn't shifting correctly. I took it to a tranmission shop and they noticed that the Throttle cable was installed backwards!!  The mechanic denies removing the Throttle cable, but I was just trying to make sure that he didn't have to.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||wwh0001||07-25-2000||11:12 AM||||I just replaced my exhaust gaskets, 87 gt. And no you don't need to, or even want,to disconnect the throttle cable. This is a job you really don't want to do unless you have a lot of time on your hands. A real pain.||||reg||1
